{"about": ["Written by make_dem_fixture.py, which says how each file was made; made_by is given only for a file it did not write itself.", "raw and elevation: what the raw GeoTIFF layer and the elevation layer must do with the file, 'read' or the catalogued refusal of spec section 2.11; elevation is null when the raw layer refuses.", "The layout keys are GeoTiffLayout's (spec section 2.3). The predictor is applied only with compression 5, 8 or 32946. raster_type 1 is PixelIsArea (also when the key is absent), 2 PixelIsPoint. ifd_index, samples_per_pixel and georeference are given only when they are not 0, 1 and scale and tiepoint.", "x0 and y0 are the centres of column 0 and row 0 (row 0 north) by the expressions of spec section 2.4; cell (i, j) is at x0 + i*sx, y0 - j*sy.", "nodata is GDAL_NODATA's text without its NUL; nodata_value is that text parsed and cast to the sample type by spec section 2.5 ('no cell' when it cannot match an integer sample).", "samples_sha256: SHA-256 of every sample, north row first, each little-endian in its own type, as GDAL reads the file with masked=False; a sparse block reads as 0 there, though the reader voids it.", "voids: the cells the per-sample rule of spec section 2.5 voids (bounds -1000 and 9000 m), when any.", "has_mask: given, as true, only when the directory after the image is a GDAL mask of it.", "sets: files meant to be read together; declare is the source the operator declares for the set."],
 "files": {
